In Default mode, Zone.js triggers change detection globally for any macro or micro task—timers, HTTP calls, or clicks. It checks every single template binding across the app tree, which causes performance bottlenecks at scale.

With `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`, Angular checks the component only when:
1. An `@Input` reference changes by strict equality (`prev !== curr`).
2. A template event listener bound in that component fires.
3. An `Observable` bound via the `async` pipe emits.
4. A `signal()` read in the template updates.
5. `cdr.markForCheck()` is called manually.

`OnPush` relies on immutability. If you mutate an object or array in place without creating a new reference, Angular will skip checking the child view.

