2. Whenever any signal read inside `request` changes, the `loader` triggers automatically.
3. The loader receives an `AbortSignal` for native fetch request cancellation.
4. It exposes reactive signals: `res.value()` (the resolved data), `res.isLoading()` (boolean for spinners), `res.error()`, and `res.status()` (`idle | loading | error | resolved | reloading`).
