### Comprehensive Senior Answer
Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) allows attackers to execute malicious JavaScript in a victim's browser session:
- **Stored XSS**: Malicious payload is permanently saved in the backend database (e.g. comment box) and served to all users.
- **Reflected XSS**: Payload is reflected in a search query or URL parameter and returned by the server.
- **DOM-based XSS**: Attack happens entirely on the client when JavaScript writes unsanitized data into an unsafe sink (`element.innerHTML`, `document.write`, `eval()`).

**Angular Built-in Protection**:
Angular treats all template values as untrusted by default, automatically sanitizing bindings (`[innerHTML]`, `[src]`, `[href]`). Calling `DomSanitizer.bypassSecurityTrustHtml()` completely disables this protection and should only be used after running the string through an audited sanitization library like **DOMPurify**.

**Content Security Policy (CSP)**:
A critical defense-in-depth HTTP header: `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://trusted.cdn.com; object-src 'none';`. It instructs the browser to block inline scripts, `eval()`, and unauthorized external domains even if an XSS vulnerability exists.

### Code Example
```typescript
import { Component, inject, SecurityContext } from '@angular/core';
import { DomSanitizer, SafeHtml } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-user-bio',
  standalone: true,
  template: `
    <!-- ✅ Safe: DOMPurify strips malicious <script> / onerror payloads! -->
    <div [innerHTML]="sanitizedBio"></div>
  `
})
export class UserBioComponent {
  private sanitizer = inject(DomSanitizer);
  sanitizedBio: SafeHtml = '';

  setRawUserContent(untrustedHtml: string) {
    // 1. Sanitize untrusted user input with DOMPurify
    const cleanHtml = DOMPurify.sanitize(untrustedHtml);

    // 2. Safely trust the purified HTML for Angular rendering
    this.sanitizedBio = this.sanitizer.bypassSecurityTrustHtml(cleanHtml);
  }
}
```
_Uses DOMPurify to strip malicious scripts before calling DomSanitizer.bypassSecurityTrustHtml._

