The core difference is top-down component re-execution versus fine-grained reactive graph propagation:
- **React (Fiber & VDOM)**: When state updates in React (`setState`), React re-executes the entire component function and produces a new Virtual DOM tree. The **Fiber reconciler** compares the new VDOM with the old one (Render Phase, which can be paused/split in Concurrent Mode), calculates the minimal set of DOM mutations (diff), and synchronously applies them to the real DOM during the **Commit Phase**.
- **Angular (Signals & Zoneless)**: In modern Angular, a Signal update directly notifies the specific DOM binding or view that read the signal. Angular does not build or diff a Virtual DOM; it updates real DOM nodes directly with surgical precision.

