> Security trade-offs: Storing JWTs in localStorage leaves them vulnerable to XSS. Storing tokens in `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict` cookies protects them from JavaScript access (XSS), but requires CSRF protection if using cookies for state-modifying requests. Also, invalidating a JWT before it expires requires a token revocation blacklist (like Redis).

